      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x+5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284523/assets/e3f5ed500c81d09e2775f09fd10a221d7ec0fca7e39249b7add7a680328b68c1.png)\n\nSince we have $y=-\\frac{1}{x+5},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ to the *left* by $5$ units.\n\nNow, since the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is translated to the left by $5$ units, the vertical asymptote $x=0$ is also translated to the left by $5$ units. So, the equation of the new vertical asymptote is $x=-5.$ \n\nTherefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284523/assets/318057e4309d1f4ee5d25549a1762c0bfea5aae460aefce8d5a1b51f6e9034d6.png)",
